<title>USA: PECO Pa. Limerick 2 nuke at 73 pct pwr--NRC.</title>
<headline>PECO Pa. Limerick 2 nuke at 73 pct pwr--NRC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>PECO Energy Co's 1,055 megawatt (MW) Limerick 2 nuclear unit was reduced to 73 percent power, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said in its Tuesday morning report.</p>
<p>The unit, located in Pottstown, Pennsylvania, was taken partially down due to a vibration problem in a condensate pump, the NRC said.</p>
<p>The company was not available for comment.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
</text>
